🔎 Text Contradiction Finder

📌 Project Overview

Text Contradiction Finder is a web-based Text Analysis application that compares two statements and identifies whether they are contradictory, related/agreeing, possibly conflicting, or unrelated.

The application uses rule-based Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques to analyze words, negations, opposite terms, and numerical values.

---

🎯 Objective

The main objective of this project is to demonstrate how text can be analyzed and compared to identify relationships between two different statements.

---

✨ Features

- Compare two text statements
- Detect opposite words
- Detect negative statements
- Identify common keywords
- Compare numerical values
- Detect possible contradictions
- Identify related or agreeing statements
- Identify unrelated statements
- Provide an explanation for the detected relationship
- Responsive interface for mobile and desktop

---

🧠 How It Works

The application follows a rule-based text analysis process:

Two Statements
      ↓
Text Cleaning
      ↓
Word Extraction
      ↓
Stop-word Removal
      ↓
Common Word Detection
      ↓
Opposite Word Detection
      ↓
Negation Detection
      ↓
Number Comparison
      ↓
Relationship Analysis
      ↓
Final Result

The system can produce results such as:

- 🔴 Contradiction
- 🟠 Possible Conflict
- 🟢 Related / Agreeing
- ⚪ Unrelated

---

🔍 Example

Statement 1

«The library is open today.»

Statement 2

«The library is closed today.»

Result

🔴 CONTRADICTION

The application detects the opposing terms:

open ↔ closed

---

🛠️ Technologies Used

- HTML5
- CSS3
- JavaScript
- Rule-based NLP techniques

No external API or backend server is required.

