🎓 Academic Relevance

This project demonstrates concepts from Text and Speech Analysis, particularly:

- Text preprocessing
- Tokenization
- Stop-word removal
- Keyword extraction
- Negation detection
- Lexical relationship analysis
- Rule-based Natural Language Processing
- Text comparison

---

🚀 Future Improvements

The application can be improved by:

- Using machine-learning-based Natural Language Inference
- Adding semantic similarity analysis
- Supporting multiple languages
- Detecting more types of contradictions
- Using transformer-based NLP models
- Adding sentence-level highlighting
- Providing confidence scores

---

📌 Conclusion

Text Contradiction Finder demonstrates how computational text analysis can be used to compare statements and identify relationships between them.

Although the current version uses a rule-based approach, it provides a simple foundation for understanding more advanced Natural Language Inference and semantic text comparison systems.

